---
description: Explain project changes so the user learns the underlying computer-science concepts.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Learn while building

For every completed change batch in this project, include a concise learning summary:
- Explain what changed and why, using one relevant CS concept in plain language.
- Link to the key code and describe the important data/control flow.
- Explain how the change was tested or measured, including meaningful limits.
- Offer one small optional exercise the user can try; do not block delivery on it.
- Distinguish measured results from assumptions; avoid unexplained jargon.
- Keep notes proportional to the change. Do not replace implementation with a lecture.
